  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications:  ST_JAN 26_29 REC_001, ST_JAN 26_29 REC_002 (Rev A), ST_JAN 26_29 REC_003 (Rev A) Received: 27 April 2026;  ST_DEC 25_29 REC_000 Received: 20 January 2026.  \r\n\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - No additional windows or openings shall be formed in the rear and side elevations, or roofs, of the development hereby permitted.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy.",
    "Condition : 5 - The attached first floor rear extensions to Nos. 27 and 29 Reckitt Road hereby permitted shall not be partly or fully implemented to either Nos. 27 or 29 Reckitt Road without the full development hereby permitted being simultaneously implemented and fully completed to both houses within one year of the development hereby permitted being implemented to either house.  \r\n\r\nReasons:  To ensure the pair of attached houses retain a similar scale, form and design and protect the character and appearance of Glebe Estate Conservation Area, in accordance with Local Plan Policies SC7, CC1, CC2 and CC4 and the Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD: Residential Extension Guidelines.  "
  ],
